<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX4-QA-005>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX4-QA-005" ;
  triage:title "C1 human-rendering contract drift in task_ledger.rs: timestamps render with +00:00 instead of the documented Z suffix and the ACTOR column width differs from the sprint doc example" ;
  triage:description "AX.4 QA-1 (quality-mgr ax4-qa-r1, PR #1194 Final Quality Report 2026-09-05T09:14Z; found by req-qa) at head aaf2e04bf. crates/atm/src/commands/task_ledger.rs renders timestamps via .to_rfc3339() producing 2026-09-05T10:12:03+00:00 where the sprint doc's authoritative C1 example (docs/plans/phase-ax/sprint-AX.4-task-cli-and-docs.md) uses 2026-09-05T10:12:03Z, and the --task-events ACTOR column renders at an 11-character width where C1 shows 9. crates/atm/src/commands/list.rs unit tests assert the code's +00:00 and 11-wide behavior rather than the doc's contract. Fix: match C1 exactly (e.g. to_rfc3339_opts(SecondsFormat::Secs, true) and the documented column widths) across task_ledger.rs, its tests, and docs/user-documents/tasks.md, or amend the sprint doc C1 contract consistently." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "ATM-QA" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
